# Placeholders only. Never put a real key in this file: it is TRACKED BY GIT.
#
# It used to hold real ones. `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY` was committed in 11a5303
# with an actual `service_role` JWT, which is the key that bypasses RLS
# entirely. A stray `Ctrl+Shift+V` line at the top of the file is what it was
# pasted next to.
#
# Two things kept that from being an incident, and neither was a safeguard:
# the JWT's own `ref` claim is `ixvwfbuvfxsijywhbbb` while this project is
# `ixvwfbuvfxxsjiywhbbb` (a different project, not a typo in the URL beside
# it), and it expired 2025-02-17. So it authorises nothing here and nothing
# needs rotating. That is luck, not design.
#
# Nothing reads this file. It was checked before the values were removed: no
# test, script, vitest config or playwright config references `.env.test`.
# Real values belong in `.env.local`, which is gitignored.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon-key>
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=<service-role-key-never-commit-this>
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_PHONE=9725XXXXXXXX
